This third Sooty_Mould image further reinforces the idea of dark, superficial growth on the leaf surface, with irregular patches. Comparing all the reference images with the test image, the pattern and appearance of the spots in the test image, which seem to be more embedded in the leaf tissue and causing necrosis, are more consistent with the second Anthracnose image (`Mango_Leaf_383.jpg`). While Sooty_Mould shows dark patches, they appear more like a coating on the surface rather than lesions within the leaf. The description of Anthracnose "Spots start small, black, and irregular on leaves, expanding into large dead areas that dry and fall out" also aligns well with the test image.

Therefore, I conclude that the disease is Anthracnose.

